  "detailed_description": "The scheme &amp;quot;Solar Water Pumping System&amp;quot; by the Renewable Energy Department, Government of Haryana, aims to encourage farmers and agriculture-based community groups to adopt clean and sustainable energy for irrigation by offering subsidized solar water pumping systems. It helps in improving agricultural productivity, reducing dependency on grid electricity or diesel, and promoting water-use efficiency through integration with micro-irrigation systems. Beneficiaries are eligible for a 75% subsidy on the installation of solar pumps.\n<br>\n\n",
  "eligibility": "\n   1. Any Haryana Resident family with Pariwar Pahichan Patra (PPP).\n   1. Farmers of Haryana with no electric agricultural connection in his/her name.\n   1. Water User Associations, Gaushalas, and community/cluster-based irrigation systems.\n   1. The beneficiaries who have not been covered under the solar pump scheme in past.\n\n<br>\n\n",
  "exclusions": "\n- The applicant who has already availed benefits under any previous solar pump scheme is not eligible.\n\n<br>\n\n<br>\n\n",
